## SQ-FCK-01 | weeds blacklisted, Rich Farmland fertile; clicks on weeds change nothing; weeds place on three soils
@group A
@commands Tag probe `#quark:simple_harvest_blacklisted`, `#immersive_weathering:fertile_blocks`; fake player right-clicks `immersive_weathering:weeds[age=7]` on farmland (empty hand, then iron hoe); places the weeds item on `farmersdelight:rich_soil_farmland`, `farmersdelight:rich_soil`, `immersive_weathering:mulch_block`
@pass weeds in the blacklist, Rich Farmland in fertile_blocks; the right-clicks change nothing; the weed places on all three soils (CR-108, CR-109 placement half)
@fails `crop_tags.js` not in the CD jar; `global.has(item.weeds)` false
@reviewed 2026-11-16
@from batches/r1113/c3_a1.qb
> cdevtest tag item quark:simple_harvest_blacklisted
> cdevtest tag block quark:simple_harvest_blacklisted
> cdevtest tag block immersive_weathering:fertile_blocks
expect verb=tag kind=(item|block) tag=quark:simple_harvest_blacklisted n=\d+ ids=\S*immersive_weathering:weeds
expect verb=tag kind=block tag=immersive_weathering:fertile_blocks n=\d+ ids=\S*farmersdelight:rich_soil_farmland
> setblock 1000 -61 1070 minecraft:farmland[moisture=7]
> setblock 1000 -60 1070 immersive_weathering:weeds[age=7]
> clear G
> pbot use G 1000 -60 1070 up
> pbot hold G minecraft:iron_hoe 1
> pbot use G 1000 -60 1070 up
> cdevtest state 1000 -60 1070
expect verb=state pos=1000,-60,1070 state="immersive_weathering:weeds\[age=7\]"
> setblock 1002 -61 1070 farmersdelight:rich_soil_farmland
> setblock 1004 -61 1070 farmersdelight:rich_soil
> setblock 1006 -61 1070 immersive_weathering:mulch_block
> pbot hold G immersive_weathering:weeds 3
> pbot use G 1002 -61 1070 up
> pbot use G 1004 -61 1070 up
> pbot use G 1006 -61 1070 up
> cdevtest state 1002 -60 1070
> cdevtest state 1004 -60 1070
> cdevtest state 1006 -60 1070
expect verb=state pos=1002,-60,1070 state="?immersive_weathering:weeds\b
expect verb=state pos=1004,-60,1070 state="?immersive_weathering:weeds\b
expect verb=state pos=1006,-60,1070 state="?immersive_weathering:weeds\b
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0
look the blacklist tag the row means may be the item or the block tag (both printed)

## SQ-FCK-02 | pack config: [dandelion_maturing] richSoilTicks = 10, fertileSoilTicks = 5 (fresh-config half: c3_ch1.qb)
@group A
@commands `grep -A6 "dandelion_maturing" config/creativedelight-common.toml` on a fresh config dir and on the pack config
@pass `richSoilTicks = 10`, `fertileSoilTicks = 5`
@fails old CD jar (defaults 20 / 10)
@from batches/r1113/c3_a1.qb passed
shell grep -A6 "dandelion_maturing" config/creativedelight-common.toml | grep -E "richSoilTicks|fertileSoilTicks"
shell grep -qE "^\s*richSoilTicks = 10" config/creativedelight-common.toml && grep -qE "^\s*fertileSoilTicks = 5" config/creativedelight-common.toml

## SQ-FCK-03 | copper pot on a lit campfire cooks bone broth from bone + glow lichen
@group A
@commands Copper pot on a lit campfire; `/data merge block` slot 0 `minecraft:bone`, slot 1 `minecraft:glow_lichen`, container slot `minecraft:bowl`; wait 15 s
@pass bone broth x2 in the output (the recipe has 2 ingredients, under the pot's 4)
@fails owner's report stands: find which recipe check rejects it (`CopperPotBlockEntity.getMatchingRecipe`)
@from batches/r1113/c3_a1.qb
> setblock 1010 -60 1080 minecraft:campfire[lit=true]
> setblock 1010 -59 1080 miners_delight:copper_pot
> data merge block 1010 -59 1080 {Inventory:{Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:bone",Count:1b},{Slot:1b,id:"minecraft:glow_lichen",Count:1b},{Slot:5b,id:"minecraft:bowl",Count:2b}]}}
> data get block 1010 -59 1080
sleep 20
> data get block 1010 -59 1080
expect farmersdelight:bone_broth
look the second data get shows bone broth in the meal or output slot (row says x2: one bone and one lichen make one cook; judge the count against the recipe yield). If the first data get shows the items under another key than Inventory.Items, the merge missed: BATCH-FAULT

